Subject: [PATCH] sim: replace existing members in macOS archives

When Make rebuilds an app object, keep a single member of that name.
Appending leaves the previous definition available to the linker.

diff --git a/tools/macar-qcs.sh b/tools/macar-qcs.sh
--- a/tools/macar-qcs.sh
+++ b/tools/macar-qcs.sh
@@ -48,6 +48,6 @@
 # https://opensource.apple.com/source/cctools/cctools-949.0.1/misc/
 
 set -e
-ar qcS "$@"
+ar rcS "$@"
 # Note: the following line is using bash process substitution
 ranlib -no_warning_for_no_symbols "$1" 2> >(grep -F -v "the table of contents is empty")
